Fetches video file metadata from the Internet Archive metadata API and downloads the best available video file to a local directory.

Exports:
```typescript
export interface IAVideoFile {
  filename: string;
  format: string;
  sizeBytes: number;
  url: string;
}

// Returns the best video file for an IA identifier (priority: 512Kb MPEG4 > h.264 > Ogg Video > Cinepack)
export async function getBestVideoFile(identifier: string): Promise<IAVideoFile | null>;

// Downloads the video to destDir/{identifier}.mp4, skips if already exists.
// Returns local file path.
export async function downloadVideo(
  identifier: string,
  destDir: string,
  onProgress?: (pct: number) => void
): Promise<string>;
```

Implementation:
1. Fetch `https://archive.org/metadata/{identifier}`
2. From `data.files[]`, find video files by extension (.mp4, .avi, .ogv, .mpeg, .mkv)
3. Priority order for format selection:
   - '512Kb MPEG4' (fast download, good quality)
   - 'h.264' (best quality if not too large — skip if >200MB)
   - 'Ogg Video'
   - 'Cinepack'
   - any .mp4 as fallback
4. Download URL: `https://archive.org/download/{identifier}/{filename}`
5. Stream download with progress: report % every 10%
6. Output path: `{destDir}/{identifier}.mp4`
7. If file already exists and size matches, skip download

Use native fetch (Node 18+). No extra deps. Max 80 lines.

